@                 Utility Bus Configuration Editor
                 --------------------------------                

Use this editor to define intramainframe configurations
for the utility bus. Intramainframe utility bus configuration is
used to define whether SYSRESET, SYSFAIL and ACFAIL will be 
imported into or exported from a particular mainframe, or both.

Field Description:
------------------
Frame: Logical address of the mainframe extender (hex)
Util Mode: bit vector to write to Utility Configuration Register (hex)
       bit
       ---
       0    -   (1 = SYSRESET out, 0 = disabled)
       1    -   (1 = SYSRESET in, 0 = disabled)
       2    -   (1 = SYSFAIL out, 0 = disabled)
       3    -   (1 = SYSFAIL in, 0 = disabled)
       4    -   (1 = ACFAIL out, 0 = disabled)
       5    -   (1 = ACFAIL in, 0 = disabled)
       6-15 -   reserved 

Usage
-----
This editor supports the following commands:

(1) list      [<index#>,[<index#>]] - lists all the entries in the 
                                      specified range.
(2) display   [<index#>,[<index#>]] - displays the entries in detail.
(3) add                             - lets you add an entry.
(4) duplicate  <index#>             - lets you duplicate an entry.
(5) modify     <index#>,<field#>    - lets you modify an existing entry.
(6) delete     <index#>             - lets you delete an entry.
(7) show       <field#>             - shows information about the field.
(8) save                            - lets you save the information.
(9) abort                           - lets you exit the editor, 
                                      ignoring the changes made.
(10) exit                           - lets you exit the editor.
(11) help                           - gives help on that editor.


@


